From b9ffcb7a6f67f60ecefd29b289dabc46b4591030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 06:51:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 87/92] dsv4 + moe-stream : SiegeLadder C7a + C7b - YoCo
 prefill (LLAMA_DSV4_YOCO=K, off by default): the decoder (layers 20-39) of a
 call keeps its last K positions before the first output - a lower bound on
 their raw windows (ring mask, P13 chunk masks, D10 per-query masks; the
 decoder layers read their own copy), whole ubatches below it run P4's encoder
 graph, and in a ubatch across it the rows below take SKIP_ID in the wave plan
 (C7b: no routed experts loaded or computed). MODE=mask - the bound alone (the
 check's reference), NOBOUND=1 - the skips alone (negative control), ROWS=0 -
 no C7b. Bitwise at -ub 1 against the mask reference (SiegeLadder
 bench/c7_check.py). Also: P16 takes up to three copy folders
 (LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_MIRROR=dir;dir;dir, the overflow to the copy with the
 fewest reads in flight); G39 draws exactly f wrong experts a call at any
 depth; G39b (ORACLE_FALSE_LOW=1: wrong stagings on q_stage_low, served one at
 a time only with no demand or right staging queued); G40
 (LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_G40=k, _H, _LOW: G35's lens stages its best into VRAM;
 measurement, off). SiegeLadder twenty-fifth session, the build of 13:5x

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
